            "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxNCzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4zgQAKdm51VmQ4LKUVx65oHQlHyr\n6UEKGXaYuSZ2QGCOrUPb3gXN70CHYERuutXCAgf7YDqECSMzoLhe+iEn0tDl+E+S\nl1M5geqyPQWFgbYtE4KvsSFbAis9mlV7kNS6Bzhi20fo+Se6O6g2cGqSx8VK99xc\n8ozNfaDbKmin/W6ntB9yL+dpFhbTctZSLwAeCm1l0N4BIOvqSEZRRynEchhP/Uux\ntAaISUYa+PCnihReqzPmU0ftZLyv0n8CgxDDqjVPwux4vp439MLVbYEwZ0dqjzOF\nW0a9z1J+isWkaWtdJ+uS9mnd+7ZW2S26MUSFApini1JmNOMv4m3C5pYwPsK6M5Ay\ndFAXcEdZQsRWIDgjZw6l9Zvxgynh9ujnsCU5IAci5TXa2bcoc5fOTX/ETnWXith/\nNcR8sDVhJJUZ91Cf6VXAHT4/NFDeznFPU430L+KBbweaAsmZOVC3AJzRtjp5g1j7\nU/wxXNLkh9twAGp4QPO3c/iwwIXTVyD8eimIReEtWsQby2qG9xtOgZ6twFln2Dr/\nT/g6hm+BKIh4NSlAkT5NmervrNFuXhQfTQbzRsOwrieWf4fqk+yY4zbaNOm/3qh5\nvEuzaLzqTrxasyC+N/eyVkp9Sj2YSV9X4M3wCL31WpGwCgFIjLrcsb98mLMOirNj\nBx5PvRI2RYA0wesIATNH\n=ys5a\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
            "payload": "tree f6e4dc54f106c090afd6a29c22520b4b28e890e4\nparent 8a5ab9b9fa4baaf48748f7b07b902b344102c3b4\nauthor Samyabrata Maji <samyabratamaji334@gmail.com> 1791283379 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791283379 -0700\n\nfix: resolve datasheet based server side model for deepseek (#7822)\n\n## Summary\n\nDeepSeek's Anthropic-compatible endpoint echoes the requested model ID back in responses rather than revealing the model it actually serves. This means the existing logic of comparing the requested and served model IDs cannot detect server-side model substitution on that endpoint. This PR introduces a `server_side_model` field in the model capabilities datasheet so the runtime can fall back to a statically declared served model when the response itself provides no signal.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added `ServerSideModel *string` to `ModelCapabilities` so datasheets can declare the model a provider actually serves for a given ID when the response does not reveal it.\n- Updated `stampServedModel` in the DeepSeek provider to consult `CapabilitiesFor` when the response's served model is absent or identical to the requested model. If the datasheet names a server-side model, it is used; a live response naming a different model still takes precedence over the datasheet value.\n- Removed the nil-guard on `ServerSideFallbackModel` assignment so the field is always overwritten when a served model is resolved, preventing a stale value from persisting.\n- Added a `TestLoadModelCapabilities_CarriesServerSideModel` test confirming the `server_side_model` field survives the datasheet decode path.\n- Added four new provider-level tests covering: Anthropic endpoint using the datasheet value, Anthropic stream using the datasheet value, a live response outranking the datasheet, and the Anthropic endpoint leaving the field unset when no datasheet entry exists.\n- Updated test constants to reflect current model IDs (`deepseek-v4-flash` / `deepseek-flash`).\n\n## Type of change\n\n- [ ] Bug fix\n- [x] Feature\n- [ ] Refactor\n- [ ] Documentation\n- [ ] Chore/CI\n\n## Affected areas\n\n- [x] Core (Go)\n- [ ] Transports (HTTP)\n- [x] Providers/Integrations\n- [ ] Plugins\n- [ ] UI (React)\n- [ ] Docs\n\n## How to test\n\n```sh\ngo test ./core/providers/deepseek/...\ngo test ./framework/modelcatalog/datasheet/...\ngo test ./...\n```\n\nExpected: all tests pass, including the four new DeepSeek Anthropic-endpoint tests and the new datasheet `server_side_model` round-trip test.\n\n## Screenshots/Recordings\n\nN/A\n\n## Breaking changes\n\n- [ ] Yes\n- [x] No\n\n## Related issues\n\nN/A\n\n## Security considerations\n\nNo auth, secrets, or PII implications. The `server_side_model` field is read-only metadata used for pricing attribution.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] I read `docs/contributing/README.md` and followed the guidelines\n- [x] I added/updated tests where appropriate\n- [ ] I updated documentation where needed\n- [x] I verified builds succeed (Go and UI)\n- [ ] I verified the CI pipeline passes locally if applicable",
            "verified_at": "2026-10-06T10:43:00Z"
          }
